 lines+=['','No raw RHO/X/OBS view had an exact conflicting-target collision in these recorded contexts. That is not a proof of sufficient useful context. All twelve identity-front OFF_257 fits remained numerically unresolved; their factorial loss comparisons are finite-fit observations. On P_SLOW/OBS the qualified full-port batch validation losses were 2.1845 and 2.3236 BPS, versus 3.8678 and 3.2634 for C16. Yet next-byte argmax accuracy was similar, so the BPS gap concerns the declared code/scale/regularization family and probability calibration; it does not establish better complete native answers. Local C16 was worse in BPS than matched batch C16 at the same budget. These findings motivate an output/write-transfer audit, not an assertion that all information was destroyed or that a larger decoder solves addition.']
